# 360walkaround/.gitignore — binaries and spend live on disk; the plan and the code live in git.
# CONTRACT §1.4. ⛔ None of these is ever hand-edited: the server writes them, and a task READS the
# ledger to state its spend delta.
node_modules/
dist/
server/ledger.json
server/cache/
server/state/
server/panos/scenes/
server/panos/probe/
# ⭐ T09 (board 360-v2) adds NO fourth directory here on purpose: a V2 tour is seeded into
# `server/panos/scenes/<tour_id>/` — already ignored above — because `server/test/no-live-writes.test
# .mjs` enforces CONTRACT §1.4's "exactly three" names under `server/panos/`, and a new top-level
# directory would have required an amendment to buy nothing. Re-create with `npm run seed:v2`.

# ⭐ server/panos/fixtures/ is COMMITTED on purpose (CONTRACT §1.4): the three round-1 2:1 JPEGs are
# $0 fixtures, and a test that needs a real equirectangular image must not need a paid call to get one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# V2 (board `360-v2`) — the Blender pipeline. Same law, one layer down: the SCRIPT is the artifact.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scene binaries: regenerated byte-for-byte-equivalent by `pipeline/build_scene.py` from plan.json
# + the pinned CC0 catalog (determinism proven on decoded scene data, not on these bytes — a .blend
# container is NOT reproducible run-to-run, see pipeline/probe/determinism/verdict.json).
tours/*/*.blend
tours/*/*.blend1
# ⭐ tours/*/scene-*.report.json IS committed: it carries the geometry checks, the frame/yaw
# convention of record and the carried plan_meta assumptions — the evidence, not the payload.

# CC0 asset binaries (~157 MB). `probe-assets/assets.lock.json` (the pin), `fetch-assets.py` (the
# fetcher) and `PROVENANCE.md` (source URL + licence + date + sha256 per file) are the committed
# truth — rail 4 / V2-PLAN §5.7. Re-create with:
#   PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8 python 360walkaround/pipeline/probe/probe-assets/fetch-assets.py
pipeline/probe/probe-assets/models/
pipeline/probe/probe-assets/hdri/
pipeline/probe/probe-assets/textures/
catalog/models/
catalog/hdri/
catalog/textures/
# the pack zips fetch.mjs downloads once and extracts from (Kenney's 5.1 MB kit), plus the
# import-test job/out/log it hands Blender. All re-created by `node catalog/fetch.mjs`.
# ⭐ catalog/fetch.report.json IS committed: it is the provenance evidence (bytes, hashes, the
# import verdict and the measured bbox per row), not the payload.
catalog/.cache/
tours/*/renders/*/pano-4k-draft.png
tours/*/renders/*/depth-4k-draft.png
tours/*/renders/drafts/cp-*/
# walkaround-production WP-03 (2026-11-01). The 846 tours' render IMAGES are not committed: they sit in the walkaround
# backup (D:/AgentTeams/_walkaround-backup/2026-11-01, sha256-listed) and go to the shared drive (D-WP-9, WP-22).
# Their records, cp-*/pano.render.json and _render-tour.report.json, ARE committed.
tours/apt846*/renders/cp-*/pano.webp
tours/apt846*/renders/cp-*/depth.png
